## Other generators

- `bootstrap:install static` or `bootstrap:install cdn`: sets up Bootstrap's assets.
- `bootstrap:layout [NAME]`: writes a layout that loads Bootstrap. Don't overwrite an existing layout without checking its contents first.
- `bootstrap:themed RESOURCE`: writes Bootstrap views for a scaffold.
- `bootstrap:cdn`: prints the CDN tags and writes nothing.

## View helpers

- Navigation: `nav_bar`, `menu_group`, `menu_item`, `menu_text`, `menu_divider`, `drop_down`, `drop_down_divider`, `drop_down_header`
- Messages: `bootstrap_flash`, `flash_block`
- Modals: `modal_dialog`, `modal_toggle`, `modal_cancel_button`
- Other: `badge`, `tag_label`, `render_breadcrumbs`, `add_breadcrumb`, and `error_span` on form builders

## Markup to avoid

These come from older Bootstrap versions and do nothing on this one. `bootstrap:doctor` reports them, with file and line, under `legacy_markup`. Plain names like `close` or `well` may be the app's own CSS classes, so check those before changing them.

Data attributes: <%= legacy::DATA_ATTRIBUTES.map { |name| "`data-#{name}`" }.join(", ") %> become `data-bs-*`.

| Old class | Use instead |
